@startuml
title 21. Keyword Search Architecture
left to right direction
actor Customer
component "Web Client" as UI
component "Catalog Search API" as API
component "Query Validator\n(normalize, limits)" as Validator
component "Search Service" as Search
database "PostgreSQL Catalog" as DB
database "Search History" as History
component "Ranking / Pagination" as Rank
Customer --> UI : keywords, filters, sort
UI --> API : HTTPS query
API --> Validator
Validator --> Search
Search --> DB : full-text / indexed filters\n(title, author, ISBN, category)
Search --> History : optional authenticated history
DB --> Rank : matching book IDs + fields
Rank --> API : ranked page + facets/metadata
API --> UI : book cards
note bottom of Search
  Filter and sort values are allow-listed.
  Query complexity and page size are bounded.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title 22. Image Search Architecture
left to right direction
actor Customer
component "Web Client" as UI
component "REST API" as API
component "Upload Policy / Validator" as Validate
component "Image Preprocessor" as Preprocess
component "Embedding Service\n(model/version)" as Embed
database "pgvector index" as Vector
database "PostgreSQL catalog" as DB
cloud "Private temporary object storage" as Temp
Customer --> UI : upload / capture cover
UI --> API : bounded multipart request
API --> Validate : auth, MIME, bytes, dimensions
Validate --> Temp : short-lived object
Validate --> Preprocess : decode safely
Preprocess --> Embed : normalized image
Embed --> Vector : query embedding + version
Vector --> DB : stable book_image_id + score
DB --> API : active book/image/price/stock metadata
API --> UI : top-K above configured threshold
note bottom of Vector
  Similarity threshold is configurable.
  Model/version filters prevent comparisons
  between incompatible vector spaces.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title 23. Image Embedding Indexing Pipeline
|Administrator|
start
:Create or update book cover;
|Catalog Service|
:Validate catalog image;
:Write image metadata and pending index job;
:Store original/derivative in object storage;
|Outbox Worker|
:Claim idempotent indexing job;
|Embedding Service|
:Preprocess image with resource limits;
:Generate embedding and model version;
|Indexing Service|
:Upsert vector by image ID + model version;
:Mark image version indexed;
if (All required images indexed?) then (yes)
  :Publish catalog image as searchable;
else (no)
  :Keep pending state and retry / alert;
endif
stop
@enduml

@startuml
title 24. Shipping Provider Integration
left to right direction
actor Customer
actor Administrator as Admin
component "Checkout / Fulfillment" as App
component "Shipping Orchestrator" as Orchestrator
interface "ShippingProviderPort" as Port
component "Provider Adapter" as Adapter
cloud "Shipping Provider API" as Provider
database "Orders / Shipments" as DB
queue "Outbox + Retry Worker" as Queue
Customer --> App : address and delivery choice
App --> Orchestrator : quote request
Orchestrator --> Port : quote
Adapter - Port
Adapter --> Provider : rates/services (timeout)
Provider --> Adapter : service, price, estimate
Adapter --> Orchestrator : normalized quote
Orchestrator --> App : selectable service
Admin --> App : fulfill eligible order
App --> DB : state + outbox command in one transaction
DB --> Queue : durable shipment command
Queue --> Orchestrator : create / retry shipment
Orchestrator --> Port : create shipment (idempotency key)
Adapter --> Provider : create shipment
Provider --> Adapter : tracking / result
Adapter --> Orchestrator : normalized result
Orchestrator --> DB : shipment and attempt state
Provider --> App : signed tracking webhook
App --> Orchestrator : verify / deduplicate / normalize
Orchestrator --> DB : append shipment event
note bottom of Queue
  Provider calls are outside the DB transaction.
  Failed creation remains recoverable through
  retries and reconciliation; no false shipment is shown.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title 25. Payment Gateway Integration
left to right direction
actor Customer
component "Web Client" as UI
component "Checkout / Order Module" as Order
component "Payment Orchestrator" as Orchestrator
interface "PaymentGatewayPort" as Port
component "Gateway Adapter" as Adapter
cloud "Payment Gateway" as Gateway
database "Orders / Payment Attempts" as DB
queue "Webhook Inbox / Outbox" as Queue
Customer --> UI : choose prepaid method
UI --> Order : checkout (idempotency key)
Order --> DB : persist order and payment attempt
Order --> Orchestrator : initiate payment
Orchestrator --> Port : create intent
Adapter - Port
Adapter --> Gateway : request with idempotency key
Gateway --> Adapter : redirect / token / pending result
Adapter --> Orchestrator : normalized result
Orchestrator --> DB : persist provider reference / state
Gateway --> Queue : signed callback / webhook
Queue --> Orchestrator : verify and deduplicate
Orchestrator --> DB : update payment attempt
Orchestrator --> Order : guarded order transition
Order --> DB : order + outbox atomically
note bottom of DB
  Never store card credentials or provider secrets.
  COD remains uncollected until collection is confirmed.
end note
@enduml

@startuml
title 26. Webhook Processing and Retry Flow
start
:Receive provider webhook;
:Apply request size and rate limits;
:Verify provider signature and timestamp;
if (Signature valid?) then (yes)
  :Validate provider event schema;
  :Insert (provider, event ID) into inbox\nwith unique constraint;
  if (Duplicate event?) then (yes)
    :Acknowledge already-recorded event;
  else (no)
    :Commit inbox record and enqueue processing;
    :Process event idempotently;
    if (Transient processing error?) then (yes)
      :Retry with bounded exponential backoff;
      if (Retry budget exhausted?) then (yes)
        :Dead-letter and alert for reconciliation;
      else (no)
        :Return event to retry queue;
      endif
    else (no)
      :Commit domain update + outbox notification;
      :Acknowledge success;
    endif
  endif
else (no)
  :Reject, log safe metadata and alert on abuse;
endif
stop
@enduml
